  <page_number>60</page_number>
  <running_head>GVISIACA</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Te rege</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">Nam veris instar vultus vbi tuus</l>
    <l n="2">Plebi nitescet pacificus tua,</l>
    <l n="3">Nubes serenata recedent,</l>
    <l n="4">Præcipites fugient procellæ,</l>
    <l n="5" para="true">Te Gallus hostes auspice Barbaros</l>
    <l n="6">Iusto lacessat Marte potentior:</l>
    <l n="7">Tuisque nunc damnis fruentes</l>
    <l n="8">Vexet eques metuendus hasta,</l>
    <l n="9" para="true">Impune captis vrbibus impotens</l>
    <l n="10">Bellum Sabaudus monuerit impium</l>
    <l n="11">Multisque quæsitas periclis</l>
    <l n="12">Vsque tuas retinebit arces?</l>
    <l n="13" para="true">Impune Gallis seditionibus</l>
    <l n="14">Centaurus audax riserit Allobrox,</l>
    <l n="15">Versámque Francorum superbis</l>
    <l n="16">Contuderit pedibus coronam?</l>
    <l n="17" para="true">Impune tectis[?] proditionibus</l>
    <l n="18">Fidens, &amp; auro, coeperit otium</l>
    <l n="19">Turbare Bernatum, &amp; vetustis</l>
    <l n="20">Fœderibus violare Gentes</l>
    <l n="21" para="true">Gallis amicas? Tunde superbiam</l>
    <l n="22">Tantósque fastus principis exteri.</l>
    <l n="23">Quis arma Francorum, tuisque</l>
    <l n="24">Auspiciis sociata, rumpet?</l>
    <l n="25" para="true">Sic dura cunctis sospes ab hostibus</l>
    <l n="26">Sana ruentis vulnera patriæ:</l>
    <l n="27">Compone ciuiles tumultus:</l>
    <l n="28">Otia redde tuis cupita.</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Uncertain: "tectis" in line 17 (the letters read as "teƐtis"); "Vexet eques metuendus hasta," has a doubled mark at the line end, possibly a comma and a stop. Ghost text in the right margin is show-through from the reverse and is left out. The catchword "Te rege" is printed at lower right; the page has no signature.</notes>
</page>
